{
 "id": "s4-l5",
 "stage": 4,
 "lesson": 5,
 "title": {
  "de": "해요 und Adjektive",
  "en": "해요 and adjectives"
 },
 "intro": {
  "de": "Viele Verben enden auf 하다 (machen). 하다 wird immer zu 해요: 공부하다 → 공부해요.\nAdjektive verhalten sich im Koreanischen wie Verben. Sie bekommen dieselben Endungen: 비싸다 → 비싸요 (ist teuer), 맛있다 → 맛있어요 (ist lecker).\nEin extra Wort für „ist“ brauchst du dabei nicht.",
  "en": "Many verbs end in 하다 (to do). 하다 always becomes 해요: 공부하다 → 공부해요.\nIn Korean, adjectives behave like verbs and take the same endings: 비싸다 → 비싸요 (is expensive), 맛있다 → 맛있어요 (is tasty).\nYou don't need a separate word for \"is\"."
 },
 "exercises": [
  "see-meaning",
  "pick-hangul",
  "build-sentence"
 ],
 "check": {
  "questions": 8
 },
